# Devcontainer pin upgrade blocklist — one <base> per line to HOLD a tool in
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile at its current `ARG <BASE>_VERSION` pin instead of
# tracking upstream latest.
#
# Base names match the Dockerfile ARG <BASE>_VERSION, lowercased: the part after the
# colon of a devcontainer:<base> id in .ci/config/pins.json (bw, bws, gopls, dlv,
# golangcilint, ...).
#
# NOTE: do NOT add an entry for a release that is merely too fresh.
# scripts/gates/check-devcontainer-pin-freshness.ts reads the freshness window from
# .ci/config/release-age.json and automatically defers anything published inside that window — the
# hold clears itself once the version ages out. Only blocklist a pin held back
# for a real reason (a breaking change, a broken asset, an upstream regression).
#
# Each entry needs a substantive BLOCKER reason (>=30 chars, no banned phrases),
# exactly like every other suppression list in this repo. Write entries with
# `npm run pins -- hold devcontainer:<base> --reason "<why>" --expires YYYY-MM-DD`,
# never by hand; it writes the inline form, and the expiry in it is read by
# scripts/lib/pins/status.ts (an expired hold stops excusing the pin):
#
#   <base>  # BLOCKER: <why this tool is pinned back and when to revisit> (expires YYYY-MM-DD)
#
# The comment-above form (`# BLOCKER: ...` on the line before `<base>`) is read too.

